{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122243","id":4239893699,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc78t6TD","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122243","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122243.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122243.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122243","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122243/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122243/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122243/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/9497808096b2c900d9c8737a0bc0fd284b886e3d","number":122243,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix fractional editor game speed physics timing","user":{"login":"siadialiga","id":193349941,"node_id":"U_kgDOC4ZJNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/193349941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/siadialiga","html_url":"https://github.com/siadialiga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/siadialiga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/siadialiga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/siadialiga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/siadialiga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/siadialiga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/siadialiga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/siadialiga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/siadialiga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/siadialiga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #122242 and closes #122217 \r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nI made similar pr hours before but it doesnt have the integer fix, so this is the new PR.\r\n\r\nThe editor Game Speed control currently quantizes the effective physics tick rate to an integer.\r\n\r\nFor example, with 60 physics ticks per second and 1/16x game speed:\r\n\r\n60 * 1/16 = 3.75\r\n\r\nbut the effective rate becomes 3 ticks per second.\r\n\r\nThis causes two issues:\r\n- `_physics_process()` can receive an incorrect delta.\r\n- The actual physics scheduling speed is not exactly the selected game speed.\r\n\r\nThis change keeps the effective editor physics tick rate as a floating-point value and passes the fractional rate through `MainTimerSync`.\r\n\r\nThe physics simulation step itself still uses the original fixed physics timestep, so changing the editor Game Speed does not alter the expected physics delta.\r\n\r\nTested with 60 physics ticks per second:\r\n- 1x\r\n- 1/4x\r\n- 1/8x\r\n- 1/16x\r\n\r\nAt 1/16x, the effective physics rate is now 3.75 Hz and `_physics_process()` keeps a delta of 1/60.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n\r\n*AI used on description in same places because English is not my native language, sorry. But i didn't coded with AI*","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","